README:

v1.00
	1. Added audio noise removal using the RNNoise method.
	2. Added audio band pass filtering.
	3. Fixed bug so that audio graph is displayed even on more narrow tracks
	4. Fixed bug so that viewport goes to the end when the cursor is moved to the end by 
	   use of "End" button.  The same when moving from the End to the beginning.

v1.01:
	1.Added an animated line drawing effect "drawlineeffect" to draw a line as a 
	  function of time through keyframe coordinate specification.

v1.02
	1.Attempted to use mouse to change points of line but couldn't get this 
	  working, so gave up for the time being.
	
v1.03:
	1.Changed name of line drawing effect to "drawlineeffect".

v1.04:
	1.Adding text effect to reveal text varying as a function of keyframe
	2.Adding text effect animation, where the text appears at the beginning of 
	  the clip and disappears at the end of the clip, works for the outline option
	  but not the shadow option.
	3.Changed some of the defaults for the texteffects
	4.Changed behaviour of track size manipulation to enable smaller track size,
	  useful on smaller screens.
	5.Added effect for privacy, for example if you want to obscure a document or face.
	6.Added a sharpening effect
	  
v1.05: 	
	1.Added effect ability to use colour look up tables (LUTS)      
	2.Added effect to draw a circle used to highlight an area of the clip
		
v1.06:	
	1.Trying another privacy method produced by gemini.  Since the Claude 
	  method gave problems.
	2.I'm keeping the gemini privacy method one since it works on both the desktop and 
	  laptop.  I removed the censor effect since it didn't work well on 
	  the laptop.                                             
		  
v1.07:	
	1.Making changes as the maintainer requested.

v1.08: 261006 
	1. Copy from v1.07 with all the latest changes.
	2. Modified the rnnoise effect to remove the echo
	
v1.09: 261013
	1. Copy from v1.08
	2. Copied new and updated effects from v1.07. Shaders: Sharpen, lut, privacy_mask,
	   highlightcircle.  CPU effects: texteffect,audiornnoise, audiobpfilter.
	   (drawline was not a part of the routines supplied to the maintainer, but it's in
	   v1.09).
	   
citrine Forked from amber v1.09
===============================
v1.09: 261013
	1. Renamed and changed to citrine logo
	2. Added option in the drawline effect to make the line speed constant over the clip
	3. Fixed a bug when doing a cut in a selected clip. The highlight color got confused when
	   cutting a selected clip which is now fixed.
	4. When cutting in a selected clip with Ctrl-K Ctrl-k or Ctrl-Z would no longer work.  This 
	   is now fixed. (However, might have introduced another bug, needs more investigation)
	5. Added facility to go to next or previous marker by using Alt-Up and Alt-Down. 
	   (I could not find a way to navigate between markers so added this.)

v1.09: 261019
	1. Added global proxy generation. Proxy size and automatic generation are set in Preferences.
	2. Proxies are created automatically for imported footage and for footage in an opened
	   project that has no proxy. Proxies are ProRes Proxy.
	3. Footage with a proxy shows a blue "P" badge in the Project panel.
	4. Replaced the per-clip proxy dialog with "Regenerate Proxy" and "Restore Original" in the
	   Project panel's Proxy menu.
	5. Set up git for this fork with a baseline commit and committed the mak build script.

v1.09: 261020
	1. Export: added NVIDIA NVENC and VAAPI (AMD/Intel) H.264 and H.265 encoders. They are
	   listed only when the GPU is available, and encode much faster than the CPU encoders.
	2. Export quality: the default is now 23 for H.264 and 28 for H.265 (was 36). The label
	   and help text follow the encoder in use, and a short note under the value explains
	   that lower numbers give better quality and larger files.
	3. Playback: hardware decoding now tries CUDA (Nvidia) on Linux when VAAPI is not
	   available, so Nvidia GPUs are used for playback.
	4. Proxies: H.264 footage is decoded on the Nvidia GPU as well as HEVC. VAAPI decoding
	   is used when available. Proxy files are deleted when their media is removed from the
	   project. The Media Properties dialog shows which decoder made the proxy.
	5. Proxy generation logs the start and end of each file, how long it took, and the file
	   sizes.
	6. J and L shuttle now goes up to 5x (was 3x).
	7. With Audio Scrubbing turned off in Preferences, J and L shuttle playback is silent.

v1.09: 261021
	1. Released as v1.09 on GitHub (AppImage, Windows installer, and Windows portable zip).
	2. Dropping footage onto the timeline waits until its proxy has finished. The status bar
	   says which clip is still being processed.
	3. The Window menu's Effect Controls and Media Viewer items (and their shortcuts) show and
	   bring the panel to the front, instead of hiding it. Previously, toggling one of these
	   tabbed panels revealed the other one.
	4. Selecting clips on the timeline opens Effect Controls. Double-clicking media in the
	   Project panel opens the Media Viewer.
	5. The main window remembers its size and position across restarts.
	6. The Preferences window remembers its size, and the keyboard shortcut list remembers its
	   column widths. The Action column is wider by default.
	7. Linux packaging uses the Citrine names. The desktop entry launches citrine-editor.
	8. Windows packaging uses the Citrine names: citrine-setup.exe, citrine-portable.zip,
	   citrine-editor.exe, and a Citrine icon.
	9. Frei0r effects on Windows are built from source, so they load on a normal Windows PC.
	   The previous download was built against the debug runtime, which most of them needed.

v1.09.01: 261022
	1. Fixed proxies that played for a second or two and then froze into garbage on some Linux laptops using VAAPI hardware decoding.
	2. Faster proxy generation with VAAPI hardware decoding. Frames are shrunk on the GPU before being copied back, which took the test clip from about 80 seconds to about 60.
	3. Software decoding for proxies uses all CPU cores.
	4. Proxy generation logs the time spent in each stage (decode, copy, scale, encode, write) to help diagnose slow proxies.
